{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/trees\/rootedtree\/reingoldtilfordlayout()"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tidy drawing of the tree: Reingold and Tilford’s layered tree drawing as Walker"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refined it, in Buchheim, Jünger and Leipert’s linear-time form."}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reingoldTilfordLayout"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Drawing","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The root is at (0, 0) and a vertex at depth d has y = d. Children are placed left to right"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in "},{"code":"children(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order, vertices at one depth at least 1 apart along each subtree’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"contour, and every parent centred over its first and last child. Where two subtrees had to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be pushed apart, the smaller subtrees between them are spaced evenly (Walker’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"improvement), so a mirrored tree draws as the reflection of the drawing and isomorphic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subtrees are drawn identically up to translation. Coordinates are "},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" arithmetic:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"separations and centring alone give multiples of a power of ½, which are exact, but the even"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spacing divides a shift by the number of gaps it is spread over, so values such as ±5\/6"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"occur and are rounded (and a mirrored tree’s drawing then matches the reflection only to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rounding)."}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reingold and Tilford, “Tidier drawings of trees”, IEEE Transactions on Software"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Engineering SE-7(2), 1981."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Walker, “A node-positioning algorithm for general trees”, Software: Practice and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Experience 20(7), 1990."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Buchheim, Jünger and Leipert, “Improving Walker’s algorithm to run in linear time”,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Graph Drawing (GD 2002), LNCS 2528, 2002.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n) time and memory, with no recursion."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees\/RootedTree"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees\/RootedTree\/reingoldTilfordLayout()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"ReingoldTilfordLayout.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphDrawing\/ReingoldTilfordLayout.swift#L37"},"conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"t